   "source": [
    "# Generate K-Means Targets for SSL Training\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook takes a manifest of audio files (presumably generated by `youtube_data_ingestion_colab.ipynb` or a similar process) and generates k-means targets required for HuBERT-style SSL pre-training. It adapts the logic from `runyoro_speech_ai/speechbrain_ssl_training/generate_kmeans_targets.py`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install dependencies (ensure requirements.txt includes scikit-learn, joblib, speechbrain, etc.)\n",
    "!pip install -r requirements.txt\n",
    "print(\"--- Dependencies Installed ---\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Mount Google Drive\n",
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "print(\"--- Google Drive Mounted ---\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Define paths for your input manifest, where to save the k-means model, where to save the .npy target files, and parameters for k-means training and feature extraction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- User Configuration ---\n",
    "# Base path for your project on Google Drive (should be consistent with other notebooks)\n",
    "BASE_DRIVE_PATH = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/your_project_repo_on_drive/youtube_ssl_data\" # TODO: Adjust to your project's base path for this dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "# Input manifest file (JSON) from the data ingestion/preparation stage\n",
    "INPUT_MANIFEST_FILE_DRIVE = os.path.join(BASE_DRIVE_PATH, \"3_manifests/youtube_audio_manifest.json\") # TODO: Verify this path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Directory to save the trained k-means model (.joblib file)\n",
    "KMEANS_MODEL_SAVE_DIR_DRIVE = os.path.join(BASE_DRIVE_PATH, \"4_kmeans_model\")\n",
    "KMEANS_MODEL_FILENAME = \"kmeans_model.joblib\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Output directory for the .npy k-means target files (frame-level labels)\n",
    "# This path MUST align with what speechbrain_ssl_training_colab.ipynb expects for 'target_label_dir'\n",
    "KMEANS_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR_DRIVE = os.path.join(BASE_DRIVE_PATH, \"5_kmeans_targets\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# SSL Model for Feature Extraction\n",
    "PRETRAINED_SSL_MODEL_HUB = \"facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h\"  #@param {type:\"string\"} HuggingFace model ID\n",
    "SSL_MODEL_CACHE_DIR_DRIVE = os.path.join(BASE_DRIVE_PATH, \"cache/ssl_model_cache_kmeans\") # Cache for downloaded SSL model\n",
    "# LAYER_FOR_FEATURES = 14 # Example: For HuBERT Large; for Wav2Vec2 base, often last layer or an intermediate one. Set to None for default (last layer).\n",
    "# Note: The original script mentioned advanced layer selection requires model modification. This notebook will use default output (likely last hidden state).\n",
    "\n",
    "# K-Means Parameters\n",
    "N_CLUSTERS = 100 #@param {type:\"integer\"} Number of k-means clusters (e.g., 100, 500)\n",
    "KMEANS_RANDOM_STATE = 42 #@param {type:\"integer"}\n",
    "KMEANS_BATCH_SIZE = 10000 #@param {type:\"integer\"} Batch size for MiniBatchKMeans\n",
    "# --- End User Configuration ---\n",
    "\n",
    "KMEANS_MODEL_FULL_PATH_DRIVE = os.path.join(KMEANS_MODEL_SAVE_DIR_DRIVE, KMEANS_MODEL_FILENAME)\n",
    "\n",
    "paths_to_create = [KMEANS_MODEL_SAVE_DIR_DRIVE, KMEANS_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR_DRIVE, SSL_MODEL_CACHE_DIR_DRIVE]\n",
    "for p in paths_to_create:\n",
    "    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    print(f\"Ensured directory exists: {p}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(INPUT_MANIFEST_FILE_DRIVE):\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Input manifest file not found: {INPUT_MANIFEST_FILE_DRIVE}. Please run the data ingestion notebook first.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"K-means model will be saved to: {KMEANS_MODEL_FULL_PATH_DRIVE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"K-means .npy targets will be saved to: {KMEANS_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR_DRIVE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"SSL model for features: {PRETRAINED_SSL_MODEL_HUB}\")\n",
    "print(\"--- Configuration Complete ---\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Script Logic: Feature Extraction, K-Means Training, Target Generation\n",
    "\n",
    "This section adapts the core logic from `runyoro_speech_ai/speechbrain_ssl_training/generate_kmeans_targets.py`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import speechbrain as sb\n",
    "from speechbrain.dataio.dataset import DynamicItemDataset\n",
    "from speechbrain.dataio.dataio import read_audio\n",
    "# Using the specific Wav2Vec2 class from SpeechBrain as in the original script\n",
    "from speechbrain.lobes.models.huggingface_transformers.wav2vec2 import Wav2Vec2 \n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import MiniBatchKMeans\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import logging\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "logger_km = logging.getLogger(\"kmeans_generator_colab\")\n",
    "if not logger_km.hasHandlers():\n",
    "    handler_km = logging.StreamHandler()\n",
    "    formatter_km = logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n",
    "    handler_km.setFormatter(formatter_km)\n",
    "    logger_km.addHandler(handler_km)\n",
    "logger_km.setLevel(logging.INFO)\n",
    "\n",
    "def dataio_prepare_for_feat_ext_colab(manifest_file_path, data_folder_placeholder=None):\n",
    "    \"Prepares dataset for feature extraction using absolute paths from manifest.\"\n",
    "    @sb.utils.data_pipeline.takes(\"wav\") # 'wav' key from manifest\n",
    "    @sb.utils.data_pipeline.provides(\"sig\")\n",
    "    def audio_pipeline(wav_path): # wav_path is already absolute here\n",
    "        sig = read_audio(wav_path)\n",
    "        return sig\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Since manifest contains absolute paths, data_root replacement is not strictly needed \n",
    "    # but SpeechBrain's from_json might still expect it or use it for other things.\n",
    "    # We can provide a dummy or the actual base drive path.\n",
    "    replacements = {\"data_root\": data_folder_placeholder if data_folder_placeholder else \"/\" }\n",
    "\n",
    "    dataset = DynamicItemDataset.from_json(\n",
    "        json_path=manifest_file_path,\n",
    "        replacements=replacements, # Paths in manifest are absolute\n",
    "        dynamic_items=[audio_pipeline],\n",
    "        output_keys=[\"id\", \"sig\"], # 'id' is the utterance key from manifest\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract_features_colab(dataset, ssl_model, device):\n",
    "    logger_km.info(\"Starting feature extraction...\")\n",
    "    all_features_list = []\n",
    "    all_utt_ids = []\n",
    "    ssl_model.eval()\n",
    "\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        for i, batch in enumerate(dataset):\n",
    "            utt_id = batch[\"id\"]\n",
    "            all_utt_ids.append(utt_id)\n",
    "            wavs = batch[\"sig\"]\n",
    "            if wavs.ndim == 1: wavs = wavs.unsqueeze(0)\n",
    "            wavs = wavs.to(device)\n",
    "            wav_lens = torch.tensor([1.0] * wavs.shape[0], device=device)\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                feats = ssl_model(wavs, wav_lens) # (B, T, C)\n",
    "                if feats.ndim == 3 and feats.shape[0] == 1: current_utt_features = feats.squeeze(0).cpu().numpy()\n",
    "                elif feats.ndim == 2: current_utt_features = feats.cpu().numpy()\n",
    "                else: logger_km.warning(f\"Unexpected feat shape for {utt_id}: {feats.shape}. Skip."); all_features_list.append(np.array([])); continue\n",
    "                if current_utt_features.shape[0] == 0: logger_km.warning(f\"{utt_id} -> 0 frames. Skip."); all_features_list.append(np.array([]))\n",
    "                else: all_features_list.append(current_utt_features)\n",
    "            except Exception as e:\n",
    "                logger_km.error(f\"Error extracting for {utt_id}: {e}. Appending empty.", exc_info=False)\n",
    "                # Get dummy dim to prevent downstream errors if possible\n",
    "                dummy_dim = 1\n",
    "                try: dummy_dim = ssl_model.model.config.hidden_size \n",
    "                except: pass\n",
    "                all_features_list.append(np.array([]).reshape(0, dummy_dim)) \n",
    "            if (i + 1) % 50 == 0: logger_km.info(f\"Extracted features for {i + 1} utterances.")\n",
    "    logger_km.info(f\"Feature extraction complete for {len(all_features_list)} utterances.")\n",
    "    features_for_kmeans = [f for f in all_features_list if isinstance(f, np.ndarray) and f.ndim == 2 and f.shape[0] > 0]\n",
    "    if not features_for_kmeans: logger_km.error(\"No valid features for K-means."); return None, all_features_list, all_utt_ids\n",
    "    concatenated_features = np.concatenate(features_for_kmeans, axis=0)\n",
    "    logger_km.info(f\"Shape of concatenated features for K-means: {concatenated_features.shape}\")\n",
    "    return concatenated_features, all_features_list, all_utt_ids\n",
    "\n",
    "def train_kmeans_colab(features, n_clusters, random_state, batch_size):\n",
    "    if features is None or features.shape[0] == 0: logger_km.error(\"No features for K-means train."); return None\n",
    "    logger_km.info(f\"Starting K-means train: {n_clusters} clusters, {features.shape[0]} frames, batch_size={batch_size}\")\n",
    "    kmeans = MiniBatchKMeans(n_clusters=n_clusters, random_state=random_state, batch_size=batch_size, verbose=1, n_init='auto')\n",
    "    kmeans.fit(features)\n",
    "    logger_km.info(\"K-means training complete.")\n",
    "    return kmeans\n",
    "\n",
    "def predict_and_save_labels_colab(kmeans_model, per_file_features_list, dataset_ids, output_target_dir):\n",
    "    if kmeans_model is None: logger_km.error(\"K-means model NA. Skip predict."); return\n",
    "    logger_km.info(\"Predicting and saving K-means labels... Output dir: {output_target_dir}\")\n",
    "    os.makedirs(output_target_dir, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    if len(dataset_ids) != len(per_file_features_list): logger_km.error(f\"ID/Feature mismatch: {len(dataset_ids)} vs {len(per_file_features_list)}. Labels may be wrong."); return\n",
    "    saved_count = 0\n",
    "    for i, utt_id in enumerate(dataset_ids):\n",
    "        features_for_utt = per_file_features_list[i]\n",
    "        if not isinstance(features_for_utt, np.ndarray) or features_for_utt.ndim != 2 or features_for_utt.shape[0] == 0:\n",
    "            logger_km.warning(f\"Skipping label predict for {utt_id} due to empty/malformed features.")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            labels = kmeans_model.predict(features_for_utt)\n",
    "            label_path = os.path.join(output_target_dir, f\"{utt_id}_kmeans_labels.npy\")\n",
    "            np.save(label_path, labels.astype(np.int32))\n",
    "            saved_count += 1\n",
    "            if saved_count % 50 == 0: logger_km.info(f\"Saved labels for {saved_count} utterances (current: {utt_id}).\")\n",
    "        except Exception as e: logger_km.error(f\"Error predicting/saving for {utt_id}: {e}\", exc_info=False)\n",
    "    logger_km.info(f\"K-means labels saving finished. Saved for {saved_count}/{len(dataset_ids)} utterances.")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Main Execution Logic ---\n",
    "logger_km.info(\"Starting K-Means Target Generation Process...\")\n",
    "device = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n",
    "logger_km.info(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "logger_km.info(f\"Loading dataset from manifest: {INPUT_MANIFEST_FILE_DRIVE}\")\n",
    "# The manifest generated by youtube_data_ingestion_colab.ipynb uses absolute paths,\n",
    "# so data_folder_placeholder in dataio_prepare_for_feat_ext_colab is mainly for SB's API compliance.\n",
    "dataset_for_features = dataio_prepare_for_feat_ext_colab(INPUT_MANIFEST_FILE_DRIVE, data_folder_placeholder=BASE_DRIVE_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "logger_km.info(f\"Loading SSL model for feature extraction: {PRETRAINED_SSL_MODEL_HUB}\")\n",
    "logger_km.info(f\"SSL Model cache directory: {SSL_MODEL_CACHE_DIR_DRIVE}\")\n",
    "ssl_feature_extractor = Wav2Vec2(\n",
    "    source=PRETRAINED_SSL_MODEL_HUB,\n",
    "    save_path=SSL_MODEL_CACHE_DIR_DRIVE,\n",
    "    output_norm=True, # Consistent with typical SSL model usage\n",
    "    freeze_feature_extractor=True # Crucial for stable features\n",
    ").to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "concatenated_features, per_file_features_list, dataset_ids = extract_features_colab(dataset_for_features, ssl_feature_extractor, device)\n",
    "\n",
    "if concatenated_features is not None and concatenated_features.shape[0] > 0:\n",
    "    kmeans_model = train_kmeans_colab(concatenated_features, N_CLUSTERS, KMEANS_RANDOM_STATE, KMEANS_BATCH_SIZE)\n",
    "    if kmeans_model is not None:\n",
    "        logger_km.info(f\"Saving trained K-means model to: {KMEANS_MODEL_FULL_PATH_DRIVE}\")\n",
    "        joblib.dump(kmeans_model, KMEANS_MODEL_FULL_PATH_DRIVE)\n",
    "        logger_km.info(\"K-means model saved successfully.\")\n",
    "        predict_and_save_labels_colab(kmeans_model, per_file_features_list, dataset_ids, KMEANS_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR_DRIVE)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        logger_km.error(\"K-means model training failed. Cannot save model or predict labels.")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    logger_km.error(\"No features were extracted. K-means training and label generation skipped.")\n",
    "\n",
    "logger_km.info(\"--- K-Means Target Generation Process Finished ---\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "K-means target generation is complete!\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  **Verify Outputs**: Check the directories on your Google Drive:\n",
    "    *   `KMEANS_MODEL_SAVE_DIR_DRIVE` (e.g., `BASE_DRIVE_PATH/4_kmeans_model/`) should contain your trained k-means model (e.g., `kmeans_model.joblib`).\n",
    "    *   `KMEANS_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR_DRIVE` (e.g., `BASE_DRIVE_PATH/5_kmeans_targets/`) should contain `.npy` files, one for each successfully processed utterance, named `<utt_id>_kmeans_labels.npy`.\n",
    "2.  **Update SpeechBrain SSL Training Notebook (`speechbrain_ssl_training_colab.ipynb`):**\n",
    "    *   Open `notebooks/speechbrain_ssl_training_colab.ipynb`.\n",
    "    *   In its **Configuration Cell** (Cell 6):\n",
    "        *   Ensure `TRAIN_MANIFEST_FULL_PATH_DRIVE` points to the manifest file you used as input for *this* k-means notebook (e.g., `BASE_DRIVE_PATH/3_manifests/youtube_audio_manifest.json`).\n",
    "        *   Crucially, ensure `KMEANS_TARGET_DIR_FULL_PATH_DRIVE` in the SSL training notebook is set to the *output* directory from *this* notebook, which is `KMEANS_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR_DRIVE` (e.g., `BASE_DRIVE_PATH/5_kmeans_targets/`). This is where the SSL training script will look for the `.npy` target files.\n",
    "3.  **Run SSL Training**: You should now be ready to run the `speechbrain_ssl_training_colab.ipynb` notebook to train your SSL model using these k-means targets."
   ]
  }
